  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Jacks or Better (Five Card Draw variant). Setup: Ante, deal 5 cards per player. Opening requirement: First player may only open betting with pair of Jacks, Queens, Kings, Aces, or better (3-of-a-Kind, Straight, Flush, etc.). Others may call/fold. Draw phase: discard and draw up to 5 cards. Final betting: standard poker betting. Showdown: highest hand wins. Objective: only qualified hands can initiate action.',
    Player: 'Welcome to Jacks or Better! This is Five Card Draw with a twist: you can only open betting if you have at least a pair of Jacks (or betterâ€”Queens, Kings, Aces, or any made hand). This prevents weak opening bets and keeps the game tight and strategic.',
    objective: 'Win the pot by having the best five-card poker hand at showdown. Betting may only be opened by a player holding a pair of jacks or better (or any hand that beats a pair of tens).',
    gameplay: 'Each player receives five cards face down. Before the first bet, only a player with a pair of jacks or better (or a stronger hand) may open; others must pass. Once someone opens, remaining players may call, raise, or fold. After the first betting round, each active player may discard up to three cards and receive replacements. A second betting round follows, then showdown: the highest hand wins the pot. If the opener split openers (discarded part of the qualifying hand), those discards must be shown when the pot is awarded.',
    keyRules: [
      'Open only with Jacks or better',
      'Round outcome is resolved by the scoring method: Scoring summary: Standard Five Card Draw scoring.',
      'Winning condition: Best hand.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: 'Two to six players; standard Five Card Draw allows this range. For Jacks or Better, at least four players are recommended so that hands are not frequently thrown in when no one can open.',
